[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## What "the reference C build" means, and why it matters
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C is compiled by the documented command, which sets no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` and therefore no `-O` flag:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cd c_src && mkdir -p build && cd build \
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   && cmake .. -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON && cmake --build .
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two observable behaviours of this library are decided by the compiler rather
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m than by the C text, so they are matched against *that* build specifically:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **NaN payload propagation.** `addss`/`mulss` return the destination
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    operand's payload, and which operand is the destination is the register
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    allocator's choice. `c2Dot`, `c2Add`, `c2Mulvs`, `c2MulmvT` and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    arithmetic inside the raycasts are all affected.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **`c2CastRay` with an out-of-range `C2_TYPE`.** Control runs off the end of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    a non-`void` function; the compiled meaning is whatever the epilogue happens
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    to leave in `%eax`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both were verified by disassembly and then measured. `tests/c_build_sensitivity.rs`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (env-gated on `ALT_C_SO`) quantifies it against an independently compiled C:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C build | `c2Dot` NaN-pair agreement | `c2CastRay` UB-edge agreement |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---------|----------------------------|-------------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | reference (cmake, no `-O`) | 400 000 / 400 000 | 2 000 / 2 000 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `gcc -O0` (independent)    | 400 000 / 400 000 | 2 000 / 2 000 |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `gcc -O2`                  | 0 / 400 000       | 0 / 2 000     |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m At `-O2` GCC reverses the destination operand of `c2Dot`'s second `mulss` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m of its `addss`, and its `c2CastRay` epilogue returns `%rax`, which it had
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m loaded with `B`. So the translation is pinned to the reference build, and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m tests are sharp enough to detect a one-instruction difference in either place.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m This is deliberate: the reference build is the ground truth.
